1
00:00:00,310 --> 00:00:02,715
Mum hid the cookies on top of the fridge.

2
00:00:02,915 --> 00:00:03,479
Grow.

3
00:00:03,519 --> 00:00:04,438
Snack time.

4
00:00:04,638 --> 00:00:05,681
Late for school?

5
00:00:05,907 --> 00:00:06,641
Grow.

6
00:00:06,681 --> 00:00:07,539
One giant step.

7
00:00:07,579 --> 00:00:08,932
Your best friend is looking for you.

8
00:00:08,972 --> 00:00:09,659
Grow.

9
00:00:09,746 --> 00:00:10,479
Again.

10
00:00:10,679 --> 00:00:11,196
Again.

11
00:00:11,236 --> 00:00:12,527
Okay, that's terrifying.

12
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:14,633
What if you could grow,
any time you wanted?

13
00:00:14,673 --> 00:00:16,475
One word, and you get bigger.

14
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:17,620
As big as you like.

15
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:18,533
Sounds amazing.

16
00:00:18,733 --> 00:00:20,149
Pigeons think you're a building.

17
00:00:20,189 --> 00:00:22,408
Your best friend gets
the best seat in town.

18
00:00:22,495 --> 00:00:24,328
And you're the coolest kid in the city.

19
00:00:24,578 --> 00:00:25,977
But here's the catch.

20
00:00:26,177 --> 00:00:29,093
Ten times taller means
a thousand times heavier.

21
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:30,238
Your bones?

22
00:00:30,387 --> 00:00:32,251
Only a hundred times stronger.

23
00:00:32,451 --> 00:00:35,816
So every square inch of bone
carries ten times the load.

24
00:00:35,934 --> 00:00:39,299
And a human thigh bone breaks at
about ten times your body weight.

25
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:40,708
Your very first step?

26
00:00:40,842 --> 00:00:41,621
Snap.

27
00:00:41,739 --> 00:00:42,582
That's real.

28
00:00:42,622 --> 00:00:45,689
You sit down on a rooftop
and wait to shrink back.

29
00:00:46,008 --> 00:00:49,210
The next morning, a man in a suit
is waiting in your kitchen.

30
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:50,742
He has a photo of you.

31
00:00:50,942 --> 00:00:51,985
And an offer.

32
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,076
Then the ceiling starts to crack.

33
00:00:54,276 --> 00:00:56,619
Upstairs, your little
sister just said the word.

34
00:00:56,719 --> 00:00:58,335
Do you run up and save her…

35
00:00:58,375 --> 00:00:59,759
or do you keep your secret?

36
00:01:03,191 --> 00:01:04,048
You run.

37
00:01:04,248 --> 00:01:05,894
Crutch first, every stair.

38
00:01:06,094 --> 00:01:07,308
Her door won't open.

39
00:01:07,508 --> 00:01:09,418
Because her room isn't a room anymore.

40
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,725
Your little sister is
the size of the house.

41
00:01:11,874 --> 00:01:12,762
And she loves it.

42
00:01:12,802 --> 00:01:15,229
She laughs, and every window
on the street rattles.

43
00:01:15,269 --> 00:01:17,629
Here's what you didn't know:
the word works for anyone who hears it.

44
00:01:17,669 --> 00:01:18,805
She waves at the whole street.

45
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:19,827
Mum faints.

46
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:20,740
Twice.

47
00:01:20,796 --> 00:01:22,938
She picks up the cat, very gently.

48
00:01:23,188 --> 00:01:23,969
Then she sways.

49
00:01:24,009 --> 00:01:25,052
Blood is heavy.

50
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:28,895
At ten times her height, her heart
has to push it ten times higher.

51
00:01:28,936 --> 00:01:31,914
That takes about three times
the pressure her heart can make.

52
00:01:32,114 --> 00:01:35,510
And without blood, a brain
switches off in about ten seconds.

53
00:01:35,612 --> 00:01:36,423
That's real.

54
00:01:36,634 --> 00:01:37,708
Ten seconds.

55
00:01:37,795 --> 00:01:39,333
There's only one way to catch her.

56
00:01:39,405 --> 00:01:40,448
You say the word.

57
00:01:40,648 --> 00:01:41,924
Your leg isn't healed.

58
00:01:42,073 --> 00:01:43,085
You do it anyway.

59
00:01:43,285 --> 00:01:43,973
Nine.

60
00:01:44,013 --> 00:01:44,669
Eight.

61
00:01:44,869 --> 00:01:45,803
You catch her.

62
00:01:45,983 --> 00:01:47,946
Then you both sit down, and wait.

63
00:01:47,986 --> 00:01:50,391
Slowly, the street gets bigger again.

64
00:01:50,741 --> 00:01:54,020
Across the street, the man in
the suit isn't calling for help.

65
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:55,170
He's filming.

66
00:01:55,210 --> 00:01:56,052
Everything.

67
00:01:56,402 --> 00:01:58,437
The next morning,
there's a card on your pillow.

68
00:01:58,477 --> 00:01:59,551
One word on it.

69
00:01:59,751 --> 00:02:00,902
And it isn't grow.

